{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-action-strategy", "file": "references/validated-grid-serialization.md", "content": "# Validated grid generation and exact action delivery

Large ARC outputs are vulnerable to transcription errors, inconsistent dimensions, and last-minute manual edits. Generate the full candidate in a structured array from the parsed test input and immutable marker list. Before submission, assert the expected row count and every row width, that every cell is an integer in 0–9, and that untouched locations retain their input values. Serialize the validated action once as compact JSON and reuse that exact string as the final response; do not copy a visually printed grid and risk dropping or duplicating cells. If the evaluator reports an invalid ARC grid, first check JSON shape, row count, row widths, and cell types/ranges before altering the semantic rule.

Serialization checks establish only syntactic validity, not correctness. Separately, normalize each demonstration by color roles and replay the same transformation against every input/output pair, including unchanged cells. Demos can vary widely in dimensions and palette while sharing an abstract rule; do not extrapolate from a single salient example or a guessed relation that fails to account for all pairs.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545531/attempts/bc528d856f1a41f1a28c3fa14e5fbbd6/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc-action-strategy/references/validated-grid-serialization.md"}
